findings.claim:
removeFrom's doc comment says that "an empty body of any type is the plain form with no field". The builder's O-022 account repeats it: 'An empty body of any type still removes'. The code refuses several empty bodies. Measured through a scratch overlay test as the owner:
- empty body, Content-Type 'multipart/form-data; boundary=b': 400, not removed;
- 'multipart/form-data' with no boundary: 400, not removed;
- ';;;' (does not parse): 400, not removed;
- '', 'text/plain', 'application/json' and urlencoded: 303, removed.
An empty multipart body is malformed multipart, and an unparseable type fails ParseForm, so refusing them is right. Only the comment is wrong.

